## How to run

```bash
source scripts/load-secrets.sh    # if API keys needed
uv run opentelemetry-instrument uvicorn {{PACKAGE_NAME}}.api.main:app --reload --port 8080
```

## How to test

```bash
uv run ruff check .                        # lint
uv run pytest -m "not integration"         # unit tests
uv run pytest -m integration               # integration tests (Testcontainers)
newman run test-data/postman/*.postman_collection.json  # API tests
```

## Key file locations

```
src/{{PACKAGE_NAME}}/             ← application code (src layout)
  api/                            ← FastAPI routers (REST)
  grpc/                           ← generated stubs + servicers
  graphql/                        ← Strawberry schema/resolvers
  messaging/                      ← aiokafka producers/consumers
  db/                             ← asyncpg/SQLAlchemy models and queries
pyproject.toml                    ← dependencies and config
uv.lock                           ← pinned, committed dependency lock
Containerfile                     ← UBI 10 multi-stage build
tests/unit/                       ← unit tests (no external services)
tests/integration/                ← Testcontainers-backed tests
logs/                             ← file logging output (gitignored)
test-data/postman/                ← Postman collections
```

## Logging

File logging writes to `logs/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.log` with rotation. Read with
`Read logs/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.log` or `grep -n 'ERROR\|Traceback' logs/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.log`
after a failure.

## Useful commands

- `uv run uvicorn {{PACKAGE_NAME}}.api.main:app --reload` — run the dev server
- `uv run opentelemetry-instrument uvicorn ...` — run with auto-instrumentation
- `uv run pytest` / `uv run pytest -m integration` — run the test layers
- `uv run ruff check .` / `uv run ruff format .` — lint and format
- `kcat -b localhost:9092 -L` — inspect Kafka topics/brokers from the terminal
- `uv tree` — inspect the resolved dependency graph
